# API standards

Versioned under `/api/v1`. JSON in/out. Stable field names (`camelCase` in JSON, Prisma `camelCase` mapped from `snake_case` DB if used).

## HTTP

| Situation | Status |
|---|---|
| Created | 201 + resource |
| Validation | 400 `{ error, details }` |
| Unauthenticated | 401 |
| Authenticated but not allowed (same tenant) | 403 |
| Wrong tenant or missing row | 404 |
| Conflict (duplicate slug, membership number) | 409 |
| Success with no body | 204 |

## Must

- Parse body with Zod. Reject unknown fields on write where practical.
- List endpoints: pagination (`cursor` or `page` + `pageSize` cap), default sort, church filter from session.
- Idempotent GET. PATCH/POST mutations invalidate nothing on the server; clients use TanStack Query keys `['members', churchId, ...]`.
- No `member_id` on attendance payloads.

```ts
// ✅
const body = createMemberSchema.parse(await req.json());
const member = await prisma.member.create({
  data: { ...body, churchId: session.churchId },
});
return NextResponse.json(member, { status: 201 });
```
